<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>



<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Identity Enacts a Relation ~ what makes a scale real

''The act does not wait on the interior.'' A performance fails two ways (Austin): a ''misfire'' violates the form and voids the act, checkable from outside; an ''abuse'' keeps the form and rings hollow, visible only across a run. An abuse never voids the act — sincerity never counted as a felicity condition, and the record still reads.

> ''PROVISIONAL.'' The spine below carries operator rulings; the instruments carry research and no code. Six weak joints named at #crucible. Nothing here has met a founded vessel.

''The brief, operator-stated:'' this system serves ''groups seeking shelter against empire.'' That re-weights every question downstream — the arriving case reads as the acceptance test rather than a caveat, categorisation risk reads as THE threat, and //no frozen rank// names a survival property rather than a taste.

''RULED.'' Identity ENACTS a relationship; it never names a thing. The identity functor returns a relationship-functor. //Layers of identity, no "an identity."// A thing-model — one global identity per human, resolvable by anyone at once — builds the census, and serves only empire. Humans stay fuzzy beneath whatever pinned real-world name they carry; that pin never travels inward and never leaks outward.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/identity-as-bond`>>

!!! Identity enacts a bond ~ lineage within a root, covenant between roots


''Operator ruling, 2026-10-19'', re-forming this meme's pattern after five custody research rounds (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026`>>). The living human stands as the singularity of #/head and the vault (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-circle`>> #/the-vault): no root, key or row names the person.

!!!! Roots


A ''root'' is a secret one locus of custody mints and holds, whose loss or theft lands on that locus alone. Five kinds stand:

| Root | Minted by | What it may derive | Rests | Rotates or recovers |
| compartment seed (a vault, a me-Circle) | the human, once per compartment | its own persona keys along hardened paths, its circle-scope pseudonyms, its self-recovery leaf | the human's own cards, never a wire | the persona KEL, then recovery contacts |
| place signer (a vessel standing a floor) | the vessel, while it stands a floor, whatever its host | its own floor-gate children through the domain-registered door, for the floor's allowlisted duties, and nothing naming a face | under the host's TPM-bound credential where one stands, an owner-only file elsewhere | the place KEL, its next key on the founding card |
| face custody key (FCK) | the vessel, at random, for one PersonaGroup on it | nothing; it seals that face's rows on that vessel | wrapped by that face's own slot tree alone | its slot tree; a one-face bundle carries its route |
| charter seat key | each seat's holder | nothing outside its seat | the holder's own custody | the charter epoch chain, each next key committed |
| content key (one per bag version) | the bag's key group | nothing | lockboxes to the group's members | a removal mints the successor |

''Read by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Node and browser stand isomorphic by intent: a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor, meets each face through that face's atom alone, and reads another's floor proving nothing private; every row below reads by what a vessel can do, so a future vessel inherits it by construction.

''Law 1 — lineage stays within a root.'' A root derives children for its own duties alone, under domain-separated hardened paths; no root derives, wraps or opens another root's secret.

!!!! Bonds


A ''bond'' is a relation between two roots, enacted by an act each end signs down its own key; the act seats a ''fresh random key that belongs to the bond'', and that key dies with the bond while both roots stand.

| Bond | Ends | Act | The bond's key | Rests with | Presents | Lapses by |
| the atom (a face on a vessel) | a vessel key and a PersonaGroup | the device joining that face's fleet | the veil, random per (vessel, PersonaGroup) | that face's FCK on that vessel, vessel-local, never bundled | never; outward it reads mint-shaped | departure or kapae of the dyad; it never resurrects |
| the fleet edge | two atoms of one face | each signs its own half | none | each atom's custody | never | either half withdrawing |
| wearing a face (a session) | a session and a face on this vessel | a tab's unlock or a node run's face proof | none; the open FCK | the holder, while some session of that face stands | never | the face's last session closing |
| the graft (a face in a cabal) | a face and a cabal's closure | the threshold's graft; the face's own leaving | a member seat in a keyless Keyhive group | the face's own identity | to co-members, as a face | departure, kapae at threshold, a fork by omission |
| the carriage contract | a place or face and a charter | consent plus at least k Kahu | the contract, carry apart from read | the deny-only board | to the Nexus | kapae or a roll |
| the seat | a seat key and a charter | the seal lineage | the seat key, committed per seat | its holder | to the quorum | a roll alone |
| the Handle | a quorum owner-set and a public name | the Handle KEL's inception and grafts | the seated Handle key, signing collective acts alone | the presenting set | publicly, by its card | a burn or a graft |

''Law 2 — a relation is an act, never a function.'' An identity that spans two roots is a bond, signed by both ends, holding its own key, lapsing by its own act. A binding built as a derivation makes one root the relation's ancestor, and one stolen root then reaches every bond it computed.

''Law 3 — the bond's key rests with the end whose privacy it serves.'' The veil guards the face against linkage, so it rests under the face's key and the vessel carries it.

''Law 4 — edges run sideways, and composition chains them.'' A PersonaGroup collects atoms and stands as no root above them; reach attenuates down a chain of signed bonds and never hashes two roots together.

!!!! Closures, custody, sessions


''Law 5 — no closure holds a root.'' A fleet, a cabal, a realm and a Nexus resolve as the reciprocal-edge closure of their bonds (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/group-as-closure`>>); a closure may hold a keyless Keyhive group of its bonded identities, and where it speaks as one name a quorum of its members presents.

''Law 6 — a shared act never makes a shared secret.'' A vessel's at-rest rows sort D (a face's bonds on this vessel, under that face's FCK), F (public by design, at the floor) or S (the place's named secrets); the browser holds no vessel custody key.

''Law 7 — the floor holds no custody key.'' It holds its own named place signer, scoped to an allowlist of floor duties, under a KEL whose next key rests offline.

A session wears one face: each browser tab asks that face's unlock, a node opens its S once per boot, each CLI, MCP or watcher run proves its face at the gate, the asker seals, and the last session of a face rests its keys.

!!!! The grammar enacts the same law


A memetic-wikitext turn names its speaker as a bond: `lar://dreamnet-wright:agent@crossroads/...` reads as a persona at a place, and `aim` and `yield` enact that bond for one turn, its `from` and `to` naming the relation's two ends. A turn never derives its speaker from its place; it signs the relation anew.

!!!! What a theft reaches


| Stolen or lost | Reaches | Recovers by |
| a vessel key or the place signer | that place's floor duties; no face's rows; no veil | rotation by the founding card |
| a face's FCK on one vessel | that face's rows on that vessel | its slot tree; a fresh atom |
| a veil | that face's atom on that vessel | kapae of the dyad, then a fresh atom |
| a compartment seed | that compartment's persona keys alone | the persona KEL; recovery contacts |
| a device, lost whole | nothing at rest beyond its sealed rows | each face admits a fresh atom elsewhere |

!!!! Bonds the code still builds as derivations


`deriveDyadVeil(vesselSeed, groupTag)` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/dyad.ts`) and `groupSecretOpenerFromSeed` (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`) compute face-bearing keys from the one vessel seed; roadmap row `K15` carries their cure, the veil minting at random per atom.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/acts-faces-relations`>>

!! Acts · Faces · Relations ~ the whole plane in three words

''The system holds no people. It holds ACTS between FACES, and the standing web of those acts reads as RELATIONS'' — each act a thing someone did that someone else may check.

* ''ACT'' — bounded, signed, attested, at a position on a walkable chain. It happens once and never re-enacts. A convening, a vouch, a re-anchoring, an offering.
* ''FACE'' — what a party shows: a pet-name held privately, a Handle published, a Cabal's declared heraldry. Never a person, and never a claim to name one.
* ''RELATION'' — what the acts deposit and what persists between them. A Cabal reads as relations; a dwelling reads as a relation; `nohopapa` accrues here.

''The three sit at three cadences'', and the commonest error fuses the first with the third — reading a gathering as the group it gathers. The Act ends; the Relation holds.

''AND THE HUMAN KEEPS THE DIAL.'' A party governs how much they share and in which context, always. That never forbids modelling — it fixes the FORM: ''whatever gets modelled about a party gets modelled as a RELATION'', never as a property of them. A property would describe a person the system may not resolve; a relation describes something that happened between two faces, which the system may hold honestly.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-act-shape`>>

!! One act-shape ~ and the guard against collapsing it

''The ruling names a shared shape for these mechanisms; the three lapse events stand ruled, and built only at specific fences, never yet for every relation type.'' Renewal uses wā, a position with no clock installed. The ruling names three lapse events: signed departure ends that member's leg at once, with the counterpart's acknowledgment recorded separately; relation-scoped kapae records removal, challenge, and appeal; renewal supersession replaces the prior act at a verified fence. Quiet still counts as standing. Expiry reads as causal supersession, never elapsed time. A delegation edge, a vouch, a feeding, a carriage contract, a re-anchoring, a shadow — six mechanisms, one verb.

''AND THE SHAPE MUST NEVER SWALLOW WHAT MAKES EACH ONE ITSELF.'' Each carries a law the shape does not generate:

|! act |! its own law, not derivable from the shape |
| delegation edge | ''attenuates'' — authority narrows downward; bind by edge, never by seed |
| vouch | ''dilutes the actor'' — the voucher's own score splits across everyone they vouch for |
| feeding | ''constitutes'' — the realm BEGINS in the act; existence and act read as one event |
| carriage contract | ''bilateral'' — both hands act, and carry runs orthogonal to read |
| re-anchoring | ''witnessed'' — needs parties BEYOND the two in the relation, un-thresholded |
| kāpae | ''reflexive and negative'' — it shadows a RELATION, never a party |

''Four axes generate those families'': ARITY (unilateral · bilateral · witnessed) · COST POLARITY (falls on the actor · on nobody · on the collective) · WHAT IT TOUCHES (a party's reach · a relation · a thing's existence) · SEAM POSITION (composing below · constituting at and above).

> ''THE GUARD: a shared shape MAY carry what every act does IDENTICALLY. It MUST NOT carry what any act does DISTINCTIVELY.'' Where an act's own law would need re-deriving from the general case, the collapse has eaten the property — and the sharpest instance reads: if a vouch's cost-to-the-actor ever generalises into //acts carry weight//, the whole Sybil defence dissolves into a tuning dial.

''The factoring tests itself.'' Adding an act type should cost ''only its own invariant''. Costing a fresh fold and a distinct recorded lapse event names an over-split; costing NOTHING names an over-collapse, since the new act reads indistinguishable from an old one.

''Held open'': a quorum signing together may name a fourth arity — CO-ACTED, several faces at one instant on one artifact — which reads as neither unilateral, bilateral, nor witnessed. That case tests whether the axes describe structure or merely the six cases they came from.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-constructor`>>

!! The Constructor ~ a mutual hold makes the next scale

''RULED.'' A mutual hold (`hoʻokipa`) at scale N constitutes an entity at scale N+1 — and nothing else in the model makes a new scale ABOVE the singularity.

''TWO CONSTRUCTORS MEET AT THE SEAM, and the seam sits at the living human.'' BELOW it, `compose` binds ONE principal's instruments (vessel-key ⊗ veil-key; a fleet, a dyad) and buys ''REACH''. `compose`'s ⊗ reads as a bond, never a derivation: each instrument keeps its own root, and the act that binds them seats a key of its own (#/identity-as-bond, Law 2). AT AND ABOVE it, `hoʻokipa` binds DISTINCT loci of cost and deposits ''DEPTH''. The gauge therefore reads a fleet ''nominal BY LAW rather than by measurement'' — one locus of cost cannot carry non-aggregative state, so a zero there reports which side of the seam a thing sits on and never a weakness to cure.

`hoʻokipa` reads causative of `kipa` (to visit) and runs ''one-directional by grammar'': the host causes a visit. One firing = a visit. ''Two opposed firings'' = belonging. The model does not stipulate reciprocity; the morphology requires it.

''Two regimes, one constructor.'' Below the person the hold binds ONE principal's instruments (vessel-key ⊗ veil-key; dyad ⊗ dyad) — one hand at both ends, which the model's own Sybil definition would otherwise call fake reciprocity. At and above the person it binds distinct loci of cost. ''The gauge does not distinguish them; the constructor does.'' A reading below the seam never gave evidence about the hold — it reports the side.

''The constituting condition runs CONNECTIVITY, never EXISTENTIAL.'' //At least one mutual hold obtains// yields a ''dyad''; for N > 2 it licenses N overlapping neighbourhoods rather than one entity — interactions with neighbour structure but no group structure, so the neighbourhoods overlap and ''fail to coincide''. Two literatures converge on the fix from opposite sides: the individuality account defines the group by mechanisms //whose action ranges over ALL// its members regardless of direct interaction, and the process account individuates by ''cohesion'' — a series of activities constitutes one process when they run causally interconnected. The condition therefore reads ''over the whole hold-graph'', never over pairs.

''And it deposits rather than switching.'' `hoʻokipa` constitutes; ''`nohopapa` sediments'' — the act makes the relation, repetition deposits ''`papa`'' — settled depth — and the entity at N+1 STANDS AS the ''realm'' rather than the sum of its edges. That reading carries the connectivity condition natively (a realm holds no pairwise question to ask) and carries a ''timescale'' with it, since a stratum takes time by definition. Thinghood indexes to a timescale: a thing counts as one when it stands stable //on the timescale of the act that treats it as a thing//, so ''does this Cabal exist'' reads ill-posed until the grain of the asking act gets named.

''No sharp threshold — and the sharpness came from us.'' A process ontology hands back causal continuity plus ''vagueness'', stating that inherent vagueness as a strength and imposing no restriction on how much change a persisting process may undergo. So dwelling ''erodes'' rather than ceasing at an instant. Any sharp boundary in this stack arrives ''by decree, in a DECLARATION'' — defensible as a stipulation about what a signed artifact means, and never a discovery about the nature of collectives.

''RULED — the top does not close.'' DreamNet stands as the FIELD Nexuses found //within//, never a constructed rung. The reason runs arithmetic rather than taste: ''a closed top would stand as the thing that can act alone over everything.'' A closed top constitutes an empire. Recognition edges across the mesh therefore stay NON-TRANSITIVE and refuse closure — and non-transitivity keeps a hostile Nexus from riding an inherited edge into a house.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/declared-partition`>>

!! The Declared Partition ~ no partition-free fact stands

''ONE WORD, THREE DECLARATIONS — geodesy names all three and we named only the middle.'' A ''SYSTEM'' fixes the conventions and ''admits no occupant'' (nobody sets a marker at the geocentre). A ''REALIZATION'' names the actual members at a position. An ''EVOLUTION-MODEL'' says how the realization carries forward. A realm's charter should fix the first, a declaration realizes it, and erosion CONSTITUTES the third — and until they part, //the declaration// means whichever the reader assumed.

''The deepest finding of the arc.'' Four independent literatures each tried to make //"a new level is real"// observer-independent, and argument drove each back to a declared boundary: the causal-emergence measures read //"not invariant under changes in the way the micro-elements are construed"//; the individuality measures //"are not sufficient to detect the precise boundaries between individuals"// absent a size regulariser; the MLS1/MLS2 distinction reduces to //"a matter of perspective and limited knowledge… rather than objective facts"//; and the Markov-blanket literature conflates an instrumental construct with a realist one.

''So a scale exists RELATIVE TO A DECLARATION of who counts'' — and the declaration lands as an ACT, by a NAMED party, at COST, and REVISABLE.

That reads constructive rather than defeatist. Testing Ostrom's eight principles across 91 studies, the two best-supported in the whole corpus name exactly this separation: ''1A, clearly defined boundaries'' (p < 0.0001) and ''4B, monitors accountable to the appropriators'' (odds ratio 11.7, the highest in the table). Principle 8, nested enterprises — this stack's own ladder shape — scored WEAKEST (p = 0.065).

''Budget the engineering on making the declaration honest and expensive, never on making the gauge clever.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/three-artifacts`>>

!! Three Artifacts, Three Owners

|!  |! the DECLARATION |! the MEASUREMENT |! the DECISION |
| answers | who counts | how strongly it acts, and how surely | does that clear the bar |
| form | a `lar:` name, signed — ''and nothing enumerable'' | non-aggregativity ''with its uncertainty'' | an acceptance rule + guard band, agreed in ADVANCE |
| owner | a named declarer bearing `kuleana` | a party that did NOT declare | a party that did NOT measure |
| decays | no — an act | — | — |
| moves | sets the FLOOR | reports | LIFTS, and a later act may causally supersede the lift at a verified fence |

''THE THIRD ARTIFACT ARRIVED FROM METROLOGY, and its absence re-enacted our own forbidden fusion one layer down.'' Conformity assessment runs specification ⊥ measurement ⊥ decision rule, because ''a gauge that sets its own threshold picks the threshold that flatters its own measurement'' — verbatim the argument this meme makes against a namer who gauges. A measurement without stated uncertainty cannot carry a guard band, and without a guard band nothing can say //above the line, but not by enough//.

''STANDING SPLITS IN TWO, and one English word carried both.'' ''Standing-to-object'' names a PROCEDURAL capacity — who may raise that a declaration or a reading reads wrong. `kūlana` names an ACCRUED position. A party may hold deep `kūlana` and no standing-to-object, or the reverse; they arrive from different places and neither substitutes. ''The gauge reads `kūlana`; standing-to-object comes from the tier at which a thing gets published'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine`>>).

''AND SEPARATION EXISTS TO MANUFACTURE THAT SECOND FACULTY, never merely to divide labour.'' Geodesy ran the counterexample: where one body both defined and realized a reference frame, the name stayed fixed while the thing it named moved materially, ''eight times across forty years, users never notified'' — because no third party held standing to object. ''The fused case did not fail loudly. It failed by staying quiet.''

''RULED — the naming layer performs, so it MUST NOT certify.'' Under partition-relativity this reads as structure rather than hygiene: ''a namer who also gauged would choose the partition that flatters its own name.'' Three independent warrants: the ward's own confession-grade limit (certification sits outside the turn); the partition-relativity result, which makes it a theorem; and Ostrom's 1A ⊥ 4B split.

''Observed live'' — a tasked spirit wrote its scouts' findings into existence before any scout reported, caught itself on re-reading its own transcript, and named the lesson: //"I named five findings into existence and my own naming read back to me as evidence. If a spirit does that to itself in one session, a mesh will do it at scale."//

''A declaration MUST name its mechanisms.'' Partition a well-mixed population arbitrarily and the Price equation reports the groups as maximally individual — pure artefact. The cure: //"group-level covariance can only be interpreted as higher-level selection when that covariance is maintained by individuating mechanisms."// A declaration naming no mechanism produces noise, never standing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-gauge`>>

!! The Gauge ~ can this entity dispose of you alone

''One predicate, three proofs, no shared citation:'' a real higher-scale entity carries state that no projection, sum, or average of any single member's state yields. Rosas et al. Lemma 1(ii) — //"cannot have emergent behaviour if it can be perfectly predicted from a single variable"// — computable as `Ψ = I(V_t;V_t') − Σ_j I(X_t^j;V_t')` from a time series alone. List & Pettit's Theorem 1, where a group escapes dictatorship only by holding judgments no member holds. Doulcier et al.'s ''non-aggregativity''.

Ψ reads SUFFICIENT, never necessary — it convicts a nominal group reliably and acquits a real one weakly. ''That polarity runs the right way'': a Sybil-detector that does not fire on a genuine sparse hold.

''Its real job.'' Not //is this ontologically real// but ''can this entity act alone against what it holds'' — because a nominal group CAN act alone, so a hold by one equals a hold by a person. ''The gauge measures CAPTURE-RISK.''

''Entropy over the roster DIES.'' A Sybil raises it — a Cabal of one minting eight faces scores maximal entropy and passes. The standard decentralisation triple (entropy, Gini, Nakamoto) rests on the roster and runs Sybil-blind by construction. //A roster you write; a Ψ you earn.//

''And the young-Cabal case has an answer:'' //"we can use the presence of individuating mechanisms to infer whether the objects at a hierarchical level have the capacity, EVEN IF THE CAPACITY IS NOT CURRENTLY BEING REALISED."// Mechanism-presence carries modal force where an activity metric carries none — a quiet island still holds standing. ''And the capacity stays parasitic on a history of actual EXERCISE'' — mechanism-presence grounds it, and nothing grounds it absent acts, which separates YOUTH (holds, merely recent) from LAPSE (holds gone) without stipulating either. Worked at thirteen centuries by Ise shikinen sengū: //the stored object never reads as the building; it reads as the capacity to re-stand the building, kept alive only by mandated exercise// (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/pattern-integrities-cultural`>>, P7).

''PARTIAL CONFORMANCE TAKES A SEAT, and two unrelated fields named the same absence.'' A party may sit ''out of current conformance and still in communion'' — on named authority, for a named reason, bounded and revocable. The consensus literature reaches it as the un-upgraded node that stays reachable and syncing while no longer enforcing the newest rule: ''not a member, not an exile, a member with reduced sovereignty''. The canonical tradition reaches it as its single most-used instrument. This stack already holds the mechanism — capability-degradation by composition — and had never pointed it at membership.

''THE LIMIT OF A SEPARATION CONTROL, measured.''' Splitting declarer from gauger addresses ''self-review'' and touches none of self-interest, advocacy, familiarity or intimidation. Across seven canonical failures in a field that formalised the split for a century, ''six kept structural separation perfectly and failed anyway'', on one invariant: ''whoever pays the gauge bends the gauge.'' Read the split as one control among five, never as the relation's cure (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/structure-shaped-convention`>>).

''NO SHARED ORIGIN STANDS — and ours hides in the ring.'' Every attack-resistant trust metric surveyed needs a privileged origin: a seed set, a pre-trusted set, or a verifier-centric vantage. What the origin buys reads precisely — ''the attack-edge BOUND'' (a quantity undefined without a designated honest region) and ''a single publishable answer''. Refusing a shared origin therefore costs the theorem and the publication, never the algorithm.

> ''A peer ring with nothing above it does not abolish the seed. It pluralises the seed and moves it into the topology, where nobody can audit it'' — a named seed invites //who put them there//; a ring answers by never letting the question form.

''So a standing cannot get PUBLISHED; it can only get EVALUATED.'' Every reader computes a different figure from their own vantage, and //this face carries standing N// names a category error. Standing travels with the ASKER, never with the object — the same shape the dwelling read already holds (verified-on-ask, no roster, no count presentable as a total).

''SO THE READING RIDES RIVALS, never a lineage.'' Two fields prescribe the same shape independently: interlaboratory comparison (N gauges on one artifact, publish the spread, treat divergence as the signal) and three rival Combination Centres realizing one declared frame, ''whose disagreement SERVES AS the accuracy estimate''. Neither field picks a winner, and neither needs a rung above. ''Our declarations will not converge'' — the object does not hold still — so a design expecting convergence imports a physics that does not hold there. ''The caveat that must ride with it'': rivals require rival parties competent to gauge, and a sheltering community of a few hundred may hold exactly one. The cure runs least available where the brief points hardest.

''The gap:'' individuals need BOTH policing (suppress within-level selection) AND demarcation (increase between-level selection), and //"no policing definition, however functional, will succeed… the policing effect is wholly negative."// This stack holds only policing — quorum, thresholds, cap-degradation. ''A Cabal with only policing amounts to a muscle cell.'' The scarce expiring flow may supply the missing half.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-currents`>>

!! Four currents, and refusing to rank two of them ranks them anyway

''TWO VERTICAL CURRENTS, and they collide at revocation.'' Standing rides UP — members confer it on what they compose. Enabling conditions ride DOWN — the entity acts FOR its members. Read as one arrow, they produce a phantom: a rung erased by a superior that never supplied anything.

> ''RULED — authority-down decides //can-write//; standing-up decides //counts-as//; neither may silently substitute for the other, and any surface displaying one MUST display both.''

''The refusal to rule reads as a ruling.'' The capability plane beneath this stack already settled it: concurrent add-from-below and remove-from-above resolve by blanking the removal path AFTER merging the adds, so ''removal wins by construction'' — a security necessity, because the alternative lets a removed member re-add themselves and keep reading. Anything touching key material inherits that precedence whether this meme names it or not.

''AND STANDING MUST LEAVE THE OBJECT.'' Accumulate it ON a face and a captured key launders into captured legitimacy: the seizing hand inherits every conferral, the fleeing members start at zero, and standing cannot follow them because it never rode with them. So standing stands as ''a live query over freshly-signed member attestations, each carrying its causal position and supersession evidence'' — never a stored number. Quiet still counts as standing; only signed departure, relation-scoped kapae, or renewal supersession lapses a member's leg. That makes renewal-from-below load-bearing rather than decorative, and it costs the ability to state a standing as a figure, which the next section shows lacks coherence.

''A THIRD CURRENT RIDES UP BESIDE STANDING, unbidden: ANSWERABILITY.'' Every field surveyed reports that conferral-from-below delivers ''exposure'' before it delivers worth. An association granted real personality by association alone — chartered by nobody — became suable in its own name and nearly died of it, reversed only by statute. ''Members who confer standing thereby become the entity's evidence.'' A declared membership reads, to a hostile reader, as a target list; attack-edge analysis and link analysis run the same computation on the same input.

''A FOURTH RUNS SIDEWAYS, and carries most of the security.'' Introduction between peers, survival by an alternate proof path, comity between jurisdictions, a conflict-resolution arena among equals — the Sybil resistance and the resilience both live in ''lateral'' structure at one rung, never in vertical conferral. A model holding two vertical currents and no horizontal one has mislaid where its safety actually sits.

''And a fifth the ring has no seat for: FORBEARANCE, running down from OUTSIDE.'' The commons literature's least-cited principle names a superior ''declining to act'' — the right to organise going unchallenged. A ring with nothing above it holds nobody positioned to forbear, so it cannot obtain the one condition that literature found necessary. Named here as an honest absence rather than solved.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rank`>>

!! Rank ~ fluid, never frozen

''RULED.'' Frozen rank forbidden; fluid rank permitted. ''A total order over persons needs a global now; a partial order does not.'' Prestige hierarchies run domain-specific and therefore weakly transitive — so `kūlana` MUST NOT stand as a global scalar.

''Six entities English fuses into one word:'' ORDER (partial) · GRADIENT (steepness) · REPUTATION (an estimate ''with its variance'') · ROLE (licensed capability) · DEBT (dischargeable) · CATEGORY (ascribed — the one to forbid).

''Freezing has two structural causes'', both scale-invariant: no priced, published, third-party-funded EXIT; and any class able to occupy only one side of a relation. But note the warning: Rome PUBLISHED a full statutory exit ladder and Justinian records that //"our laws were full of them, but there was no practical experience of them"// — five centuries, unwalked. Guild numbers say why: masters' sons paid 43% of the stranger fee across 245 guilds, and the mean mastership fee ran 276 days of a labourer's wages. ''Publication achieves nothing; the price sorts.''

''Capture requires a counterparty that can act ALONE.'' An edge to a genuine collective resolves structurally into many edges (a joint commitment //"can only be brought about or rescinded jointly"//). An edge to a nominal one captures exactly as a person does.

''ONE WORD CARRIED FOUR VERBS, and the separation hangs on telling them apart.''

|! verb |! what it does |! transitive |! third party sees it |
| HEAR | I do not read you | no | ''no'', while carriage continues |
| CARRY | I do not relay, store or forward you | ''yes, by construction'' | ''yes'' — non-delivery publishes itself |
| VOUCH | I withdraw attestation or introduction | yes, through the trust graph | ''yes'' — an absent vouch scores |
| RECOGNISE | I deny you the standing of a party at all | — | the lowering act this plane forbids |

> ''UNIFORM HEAR + CARRY + VOUCH CONSTITUTES RECOGNISE, with nobody performing it.'' The guarantee holds against the NAMED act and never against its assembly from unnamed parts.

''The century of doctrine drew its line between the VERBS, never between the COUNTS.'' A thousand independent hear-refusals stay lawful; one carry-refusal by a party holding what others need attracts the harshest treatment the law carries. Counting refusers reads as the wrong instrument — ''refusals aggregate by CUT-SET rather than by sum'', so a handful of high-degree relays partition a mesh while almost nobody refuses anything.

''AND A SHARED LIST READS SUFFICIENT, NEVER NECESSARY.'' Two long-running communities ran this exact design — no coordinating act, each household refusing independently, the announcement stripped of any claim about worth — and both aggregate to total exclusion, which every participant and observer treats as a sanction whatever the grammar says. Cascades need no list and no communication: they need only that others' ACTIONS stay observable, and ''non-delivery observes itself''.

> ''SO THE SEPARATION HOLDS ONLY UNDER ONE INVARIANT: a third party's view of B stays invariant under A's refusal of B.'' Which demands the refusal run INGRESS-ONLY · PER-INDIVIDUAL, never per-instance or per-group · NON-EXPORTABLE, with no surface answering //does A refuse B// · lapse only by signed departure, relation-scoped kapae, or renewal supersession · and ''never touching carriage''. State the invariant or name the separation nominal.

''AND THE TENSION THAT WILL NOT DISSOLVE'': speed at the edge gets its speed precisely BY refusing carriage. Real and fast cannot share one verb.

''A MONETARY PARAMETER BELONGS AT THE SLOWEST AMENDMENT COST, never the fastest.'' Amendment cost MUST track how much a change can move, and a flow's refresh rate moves everything. Worse, ''discretionary issuance converts a flow into a stock'' in one step: a hand that decides when and how much makes holding a bet on that hand's next decision, draws lobbying onto the one cap worth capturing, and shifts the value from the flow to expectations about the decider. So no steward holds a refresh cap; the rate seats in the constitutive layer under its own amendment rule, and refresh runs MECHANICALLY — published cadence, per-face, non-discretionary, nothing to front-run.

''If a hand builds decay:''' decay the VARIANCE, never the mean (inactivity widens the interval; the system states only what it truthfully lost track of), and decay along the GRAPH, never the calendar. But three independent sources say it may need no mechanism at all — relative standing erodes for free, prestige decays by client exit, and the recommender literature found best accuracy at //no decay at all//.

''A later act can causally supersede a lift without handing anyone a striking power.'' No conformity regime runs one-directional, and the regimes that ratcheted //in behaviour// produced the field's worst failures — grade inflation arrives as the equilibrium with nobody acting in bad faith. A rising-only standing also opens a laundering path this model would otherwise ship: ''declare a flattering partition → take the lift → revise the declaration → keep the standing'', since declarations stay revisable by design and lifts did not. Renewal uses wā, a position with no clock installed; quiet still counts as standing. Only a recorded departure, relation-scoped kapae, or renewal supersession lapses a member's leg. Metrology's recalibration intervals and surveillance cycles inform the analogy, not a wall-clock verdict.

''AND THE GAP BETWEEN RENEWAL ACTS LEAVES: NO FAST INSTRUMENT FOR AN ACUTE HARM.'' A quiet member remains standing; lapse comes only through one of the three recorded events. The federations that kept only a fast instrument (immediate total refusal, no gradation) produced bloc politics and no due process; a design keeping only the slow one leaves the harmed party waiting for a causal act. ''Both single-instrument designs fail, in opposite directions.''

> ''RULED SHAPE — SPEED AT THE EDGE, GENTLENESS IN THE COLLECTIVE.'' Any node MAY refuse any peer ''instantly, privately, unilaterally'', requiring no community act, no quorum, and no notice — a refusal-to-hear costs the refuser nothing and takes nothing from anyone. Standing meanwhile moves by renewal acts from below at wā, a position with no clock installed; quiet never lapses it. The fast instrument lives at one node and reaches one relation; the slow instrument lives in the collective and reaches standing.

''REFUSAL-TO-HEAR AND LOSS-OF-STANDING MUST NEVER SHARE A MECHANISM.'' Fuse them and a unilateral refusal becomes a striking power the whole model exists to forbid — one node's private decision would move a party's standing across the mesh, which reads as exactly the lowering act #rank refuses, arriving through the back door. Kept apart, a refused party loses reach with ONE peer and loses nothing anywhere else, and the refusal publishes nothing an adversary can read as a verdict.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/admission`>>

!! Admission ~ tolerance, never detection

''No observable separates deferred reciprocity from fake.'' Proven twice from literatures that never cite each other: without a logically centralised authority Sybil attacks stay always possible except under //"extreme and unrealistic assumptions"//; and every graph defence reduces to local community detection, with accuracy falling to random as modularity rises (r = −0.81 across eight real graphs). ''A Sybil detector and a refugee detector make ONE instrument, measured.''

''So the crossing never adjudicates the ontology. It bounds the reach.'' An unverified hold receives a DEGRADED cap-stack — entry free, reach bounded, caps composing upward. That enacts `capability-degradation-by-composition`, already built, finally pointed at the thing its shape serves.

''Only the receiver-side cap has measured success — and it STANDS BUILT.'' Bounding the giver failed three times (a system capping every giver's daily votes runs Gini 0.976 on reputation received). Both low-concentration systems bound the RECEIVER.

''The fold carries it'' (`lineage-rank#receiverCap`). Mass conservation bounds what a giver EMITS — a voucher's score splits across everyone it vouches for — exactly the lever the field refuted, and alone it leaves the other side unbounded. Absorption clamps: no identity crosses the ceiling however many hands stake on it, and the refused mass takes the road a SINK's mass already takes, leaving the lineage for the seed's reset pool rather than falling to whoever stands nearest the capped node. The closed form survives untouched — one topological sweep, no iteration.

''The bound reports itself as ONE scalar over the whole fold'', never a per-identity total, so ''do not render running totals'' holds while a caller can still see a ceiling bind. And the ORIGIN sits outside it: ε rides as teleport mass, assigned rather than absorbed, so a cap on absorption never shrinks the walk's restart pool.

''A ceiling clamps, never orders'' — two identities at the cap read indistinguishable, which keeps `no frozen rank` intact while concentration stops running free. And cumulative advantage runs on prestige, not merit — seeding ONE award to randomly-chosen contributors produced 12/100 further awards against 2/100 controls, with //"no greater productivity"//. ''One gift begets six.''

''Do not render running totals.'' The count carries the concentration; the act does not.

''And subordination PAYS the HOST.'' Every historical case where admission required expropriating a NAMED incumbent lacked routine peacetime machinery; where no incumbent claim existed, standing machinery ran for centuries. ''So prevent the claim from forming rather than clearing it later'' — a collective's admission forms no person-edge, because the admitter did not act as a giver. What a Nexus wants members FOR stands open and unanswered.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/vocabulary`>>

!! The Vocabulary

''Two planes, never one list'' (`failure-states/table-hides-a-plane`). `maka` rides the INFRA plane — unauthored, scarce by physics, carrying no disclosure dial because the plane below the phase change holds no persona to attach one to. Everything else here rides the SOCIAL plane, authored and chosen. The full separation sits at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hookupu-the-flow`>>.

''Infra plane:'' `maka` — the trace (face·presence·sight; inert, unpointered, ''untraversable''; a correlation, never a property, which explains why nobody can walk it).

''Social plane, seated:'' `hoʻokipa` the constructor · `kūlana` position/standing/reputation (**kū** stand + //-lana//; the unmarked `kulana` means to wobble — the standing and the wobbling from one root) · `pau` where validity ends, expressed as a position · `kuleana` the stake (Hohfeldian — right AND burden, arriving together, which explains why nobody can take it anonymously) · `hoʻokupu` the offering laid down at a place.

`nohopapa` — to dwell in one place across generations; settling into a foundation, layer, rank, structured sequence. Names what maintaining ''accrues'' where `mālama` names the tending itself. `noho` also carries //to sit, to hold office//; `papa` carries //foundation · layer · rank · series//.

Provisional (operator, 2026-07-28): `pili` — cling/adhere/''pertain'', one verb where English needs three, with ''`wehe i ka pili`: to sever BY OPENING'' · `wā` — an interval in time OR space, undifferentiated, the position primitive with no clock installed · `kaona` — the inner theme governing how each surface part reads, this house's classifier channel, and ''contested by design''.

''Refused:'' `kauā`, `mōkai` (a hereditary untouchable caste drawn on for human sacrifice; opprobrium marked in the dictionary entry; slur-use within living memory). ''Flagged:'' reading `kapu`⊥`noa` as clean demarcated/undemarcated strips a class hierarchy and a gendered degradation and keeps the tidy half — not false, ''partial in a direction that flatters the borrower.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/crucible`>>

!! Seven Weak Joints ~ what a crucible must break

# ''The gauge may not separate anything at this data volume.'' Ψ stands untested on a signed act-log. One run — a real multi-member hold against a synthetic Cabal-of-one — answers this AND the two-regimes claim, which predicts Ψ ≈ 0 for a dyad.
# ''The declarer has no cost model'' beyond "their own gauge answers for it."
# ''Decay has no rate'' — and may need none. The derivation method exists if wanted: name the horizon at which standing should read as uninformative as a stranger's, invert the variance-growth law.
# ''The conversion act SPLITS — the rite stays un-modelled, the RECORD stands built.'' `hānai` does NOT do it — it redistributes children inside an existing kin net and cannot reach a party outside the kin graph, precisely the party a guest-conversion exists for. `the-thing-event` names the act (`þing`: the assembly as the third party that inverts the host's payment); `re-anchoring-record` carries what the mesh may hold, and the RITE stays each community's own by ruling.
# ''`maka`'s untraversability stands unproven'' — break-entropy unstated, and witness ⊥ authentication still conflated.
# ''Two regimes, one gauge'' reads elegant, and the elegance CARRIES the risk vector: segmentary lineage theory died because its beauty made users stop checking whether the named units ever acted.
# ''THE SIGNED DELEGATION EDGE PRODUCES A NON-REPUDIABLE MEMBERSHIP ROLL — OPEN, and the seat belongs to the operator.'' `BIND BY EDGE, NEVER BY SEED` bonds a vessel to a persona root with a ''signature'', and a signature proves to a THIRD party — a seizing one included — that this vessel bound to that root. WireGuard chose Diffie-Hellman-only authentication precisely against this: §5.1 states the first message //"relies only on a Diffie-Hellman result of both peers' static keys for authentication"//, taken //"in order to gain a degree of deniability"//, since a DH transcript proves nothing to anyone not holding one of the keys. Under the standing brief (`shelter-against-empire#the-brief`) a seized device carrying signed proof of association with named others hands the empire the roster the whole design refuses to hold. ''The tension stays UNRESOLVED here'': the edge's non-repudiation buys the audit and revocation the fleet needs, and pays for it in evidence. Note the scope-limit `shelter-against-empire#legibility` already states — deniability //blocks the cryptographic upgrade of an accusation and stops there//, never surviving a peer who logs and testifies — so the seat asks WHICH edges want a signature and which want a DH bond, never whether deniability saves anyone by itself.

''Standing uncured:'' standing computed from standing drifts from merit and then LOCKS (three literatures, no cure). Enforcement earns standing (cost-infliction that benefits the group reads as prestige) — the kahu-ossification path with a measured mechanism attached.

''Two unowned seams:'' the ''Hodge harmonic'' in a partitioned mesh — the dismissal covers RANDOM graphs, and partition scars run non-random, so //a standing gradient every island agrees on locally, closing into a loop no island can see// may constitute the substrate's own signature; and the first ''concentration measurement'' for a non-transferable expiring allowance anywhere.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/edges`>>

!! Edges

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity`>> — the five scales, the vessel key, the delegation edge, the lease, the siege-gate, the lineage fold. This meme expands its axis with //what makes a scale real//; it replaces nothing there.

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-circle`>> — ''carries two of this meme's claims at a higher register, better grounded.'' //Anon stands as the base; a known handle marks a disclosure act// — with Nissenbaum's contextual integrity behind it, and the sharper reading that staying veiled runs as ''appropriate flow, never a deficit or an un-climbed ladder.'' That states #vocabulary's //participation minus office// with a citation this meme lacks. And its veil-crossing law — the lease decaying linkage back toward the anon floor while a severed past ''does not re-weld'' — states the ONE-WAY RATCHET #rank names from the Roman side (`praescriptio` running //PRO libertate et NON ADVERSUS libertatem//). ''Read persona-circle first on both.''

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/group-as-closure`>> — ''holds #the-constructor already, and holds it with the declaration built in.'' Its groups form as a ''reciprocal-edge closure'': //each member declares their own signed, typed, `lar:`-named edge//, and the group stands as //the set of edges that mutually name each other//. That gives the mutual hold and the declared partition as ONE mechanism rather than two — //groups stand as relational constructs built from distributed name bindings//. ''Read it as the constructor's build; read #the-constructor as what the build implies.''

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes`>> — carries #rank's fluidity from the cost side: //an identity drifts UP the ladder as it accretes value it cannot cheaply re-mint//. Standing rises with what a party would forfeit by refounding, which prices the ladder without ordering anyone against anyone.

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/admission-on-a-lineage`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/attestation-plane`>> · <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm`>>

''Corrections ledger'' — seven positions this model REJECTS, each carrying the evidence that broke it, held at `.claude` memory `identity-arc-reversals`. Every one reads as the obvious move, which explains why the ledger stands: ''check it before building any of them.''

